Subject: [PATCH] Molten Core: melee step off a Majordomo add with Damage Shield

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

Every 30 seconds Majordomo Executus casts either Magic Reflection (20619) or
Damage Shield (21075) on himself and the adds around him. While an add carries
Damage Shield, every melee swing into it hurts the attacker. The moltencore
strategy only keeps damage off Majordomo himself, so melee bots keep swinging
into a shielded Flamewaker Healer (11663) or Flamewaker Elite (11664). This is
patch 2 of 4 for the encounter and builds on patch 0017, which edits the same
function.

WHAT IT DOES

For a melee bot's damage target selection, an add that carries Damage Shield
is excluded in the same hook that already excludes Majordomo and the reflecting
adds. The bot then takes another add that is not shielded, or has no target and
waits until the aura drops. The aura id 21075 is SPELL_DAMAGE_REFLECTION in the
core's Majordomo script.

Melee bots have no timeout fallback: they wait out the shield window, which
relies on the Damage Shield aura expiring. A live Majordomo run confirms it.

WHAT THIS PATCH DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO

It does not touch casters (Magic Reflection is patch 0017), the kill order
(patch 3) or the threat after Teleport Target (patch 4). It selects on the DPS
target exclusion only, so tanks keep their own target selection. It keys on the
aura by spell id on the two add entries only, so no other encounter is
affected.

WHEN THIS PATCH SHOULD BE DELETED

When the fork's Molten Core strategy keeps melee off a Damage Shield target
itself.

diff --git a/src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCHelpers.h b/src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCHelpers.h
index 1bc12c3..2b9a1aa 100644
--- a/src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCHelpers.h
+++ b/src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCHelpers.h
@@ -35,6 +35,8 @@ enum MoltenCoreSpells
     // Majordomo Executus: every 30s he casts this on himself and the adds
     // around him
     SPELL_MAGIC_REFLECTION = 20619,
+    // The other half of the same cast: melee hitting its holder is hurt.
+    SPELL_DAMAGE_REFLECTION = 21075,
 };
 
 constexpr uint32 MAGMA_SPLASH_BACK_OFF_STACKS = 20;
